# 🔹 Multiple Decorators

A function can have more than one decorator.

```python
@decorator1
@decorator2
def function():
```

Conceptually, Python executes:

```text
function = decorator1(decorator2(function))
```

Execution order:

```text
Decorator 1 → Before
       ↓
Decorator 2 → Before
       ↓
Original Function
       ↓
Decorator 2 → After
       ↓
Decorator 1 → After
```

---

## Problem 4 — Start and End Decorators

```python
def first(function):
    def wrapper():
        print("------------Start----------")
        function()
    return wrapper


def second(function):
    def wrapper():
        function()
        print("----------End-----------")
    return wrapper


@first
@second
def name():
    print("Hello Manoj")


name()
```

